  <!-- SKILLS DEMAND -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>Skills Demand & Future-Proofing</h2>
    <p>Skill demand scores have remained relatively stable across the horizon, but the composition of in-demand skills is shifting. Technical depth — particularly in AI/ML infrastructure, security, and cloud platforms — correlates with lower automation risk and stronger survival prospects.</p>

    <div class="chart">
      <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['skill_demand_trend']}" alt="Skill Demand Trend">
    </div>

    <div class="insight-box">
      <strong>Skill Stability:</strong> Despite automation headwinds, average skill demand scores for top competencies (Python, Deep Learning, Java, SQL, AWS) have held in the 75–85 range across the full period. This indicates that employers continue to value these skills even as the tasks performed with them evolve.
    </div>

    <h3>Skill Demand & Risk Profile</h3>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Primary Skill</th><th>Avg Demand Score</th><th>Typical Role Risk</th><th>Future-Proofing Verdict</th></tr>
